---
import ProductFigure from "../ui/ProductFigure.astro";
import SectionHead from "../ui/SectionHead.astro";
import AutopilotView from "../views/autopilot/AutopilotView.astro";
import "./Autopilot.css";
---

<section id="autopilot" class="section autopilot" aria-labelledby="autopilot-title">
  <div class="wrap-wide">
    <div class="autopilot-head">
      <SectionHead eyebrow="Autopilot" id="autopilot-title">
        <Fragment slot="title">When a step ends, Autopilot starts the next agent.</Fragment>
      </SectionHead>
      <div class="autopilot-copy">
        <p>
          Autopilot has one rule for each task event, and you turn on the rules that you want. When
          the spec is ready, the Planner starts. When the plan is ready, the Builder starts. When
          the build is done, QA starts. When QA rejects the build, the Builder gets the QA report.
          When QA approves, the Builder opens a pull request. Only you can approve a task.
        </p>
        <p class="split-note">
          Autopilot reacts only to the events that it sees while the app is open. An agent can still
          stop to ask you a question or to get approval for a command.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <ProductFigure caption={["Kanban Board", "Autopilot rules on"]}>
      <AutopilotView />
    </ProductFigure>
  </div>
</section>
